ument  performance  now quality cases are not  just the domain of biotechnology  instrumentation it has been accepted in  a multitude of business segments ranging  from aerospace  food processing and silicone chip  manufacturing  even package shipping adopted  qualification  an example is amazon  when they build out a local warehouse  they install what is called a conveyance  system to move more move orders from  fulfillment to logistics for delivery  they perform a qualification of the  conveyance system and computer system  validation of the software and computers  that employees use to process your  orders  our thermo fisher scientific  qualification  documents that the instrument is  installed  operating and performing to the  manufacturer's design specifications it  is performed by a trained and certified  service engineer such as myself and you  will receive a document as well as  supporting attachments  as we have mentioned qualifications are  an industry standard accepted in  response to regulations  what would be an example of such  regulations directly applicable to  thermo fisher scientific customer  and our instrumentation is quality  system requirements of productions and  process controls and process validation  if we dig deep into  820.70g it defines the essentials of  what equipment performance needs to be  documented  we have highlighted the pertinent  language  that guy that guidance interprets for  the industry  again it's not calling out the iqopq  mechanism but rather what needs to be  documented  subsections for maintenance inspection  adjustment of equipment are specific to  each manufacturer's recommendation and  design  for one the maintenance schedule each  manufacturer shall establish and  maintain schedules and records for the  adjustment cleaning and other  maintenance of the equipment to ensure  that manufacturing specifications are  met  maintenance activities include the date  and individuals performing the  maintenance activities shall be  documented for two inspection  each manufacturer shall conduct periodic  inspections and records in accordance  with established procedures to ensure  adherence to applicable equipment  maintenance and schedules  the inspections include the date and  individuals conducting the inspections  should be documented  number three  adjustment each manufacturer shall  ensure an inherent limitations or  allowable tolerances and records are  visibly posted on or near the equipment  when a new laboratory equipment or  instrumentation is installed into a  workflow an iq oqpq should be  the  performed  of equipment instrumentation and  associated software is an integral part  of the process validation here is a  specific code of federal regulation  sections of prop for process validation  this code of federal regulation and the  complementary iso standards applicable  for medical devices  13485 require that validation of a  process particularly manufacturing shall  be performed  we have highlighted some of the  important  language that  guidance documents help interpret  subsection a calls out the process  validation need to be done that needs to  be done for example where results cannot  be fully verified subsection b calls out  details of who what how and when of a  process foundation  qualified individuals shall be  documented  in stated requirements with a process to  review and evaluate reinvalid  where appropriate  for perspective to better understand  subsection b we have provided provided  the fda quality systems definition of  establish  establish means define document and  implement  the objective of  validation is to produce that documented  evidence provide a high degree of  confidence to or assurance that all  parts in scope will consistently  function according to specification when  called into use  so what does process validation look  like here is a high level overview  there could be a lot of steps detailed  but here are have here we have a few  broken out into major milestones  any validation starts with the  development of a plan  for  for our purposes this would move into  the qualification of hardware and  instrumentation data is collected and  organized into validation report  and if  the plan inputs are met the workflow is  it is in specification and can be  released  the objective of qualification is to  produce documented evidence  that an instrument is in a workflow is  performing within the manufacturer's  design specification again we want to  emphasize the documentation process here  now that we've established the industry  standard origin of the qualification  from within regulations and standard for  process validation we can move into what  a qualification is  as most of you will be familiar there  are three components to a qualification  installation operational and performance  notice an additional box below pq on the  slide  here is where thermo fresher scientific  life sciences group differentiates ruo  and the ibd dx instrument products the  pq is performed with the dx or ibd  instruments and the ipv or instrument  performance verification  is performed with the ruo instruments to  be clear  for our audience this is strictly  thermo-fisher's scientific nomenclature  to differentiate our intermutation  for our purposes they are equivalent all  three components make a completed  qualification protocol  we will be speaking in more detail of  each of the qualification components as  well as  the difference between hardware pq and  workflow pq  moving on to the details the first  component of the qualification is  installation by definition the  installation qualification will  establish confidence that process  equipment and ancillary systems are  installed to the manufacturer's  recommendations  additional supporting details about  installation instruction and test  procedures can be found in section  820.170 installation  what does thermal scientific interpret  this to mean for the instrument  iq  it means we will verify and document  instrument or equipment against order  invoices any specific site requirements  any configuration details of the  instrument or equipment and specific  install criteria  it should be noted that  iq or installation qualification is not  repeated once the instrument or  equipment is successfully installed  follow-up qualifications would be called  oqpq  component 2 of the qualification is  operational by definition the  operational qualification  will establish confidence that process  equipment and ancillary systems are  capable of consistently operating within  the manufacturer's established limits of  specification and tolerances  additional supporting additional  supporting detail can be found in 820.72  inspection  measuring and test equipment  820.80 except acceptance activities and  subpart n 820.200  servicing  thermo-fisher scientific breaks down the  operational section into effective  subsystems of our instrument and  equipment  some examples of subsystem testing are  the internal self-test diagnostics  thermal testing  lamp or laser alignments  and  optical calibrations  final component of qualification is  performance qualification or instrument  performance verification  remember thermoscientific uses pq ports  dx or ibd instruments and ipv for its ru  instruments  by definition the performance  qualification or instrument performance  verification  will establish confidence that process  equipment and ancillary systems are  performing to the manufacturer's  recommendations by demonstration with  objective results  now this might be a bit confusing the  most common understanding of a pq is  of a pq or performance qualification is  the established limits and  specifications for the entire workflow  that were processed including equipment  instruments and software in the case of  thermal fissure scientific the  instrument hardware qualification the pq  component is focused on the workflow of  our instrument hardware not as the  larger workflow or process pq that the  instrument is being used in  our hardware pq establishes the utility  of the instrument and the standard  independently from  its suitability for the use of the total  process workflow  thus  the thermo fisher scientific instrument  hardware qualification becomes a  supporting element in the larger process  validation  unfortunately thermofister cannot  perform the process validation for you  some examples of hardware pq or ipv  standards thermo fisher scientific uses  in its instrumentation are an rna p  plate for quantitative pcr instruments  sequencing and g gene scan standards for  ce or capillary electrophoresis  instruments  and control beads or other synthetic  controls in our ngs or next-gen  sequencing products  now that we know what a qualification is  we can ask when are qualifications  required  all qualifications are recommended upon  installation or relocation after any  significant repair  post completion of planned maintenance  after any configuration changes such as  software revisions or hardware upgrades  and if the laboratory use changes  as moving from away from research into  sample processing or research into a  clinical environment  thermo fisher scientific uses a  risk-based approach in alignment with  fda philosophy to make recommendations  to customers after any critical or  significant repairs  let me provide an example  if a fuel service engineer replaces a  door or hinge and has nothing to do with  the  the  instrument operation or or the way it  generates data  then we would not recommend a  revalidation however if we replace a  halogen lamp that would affect  fluorescence or the  light path  would impact the data we would recommend  every qualification  why are qualifications important  qualifications are important documented  evidence as performance over time as we  have established in the previous slide  qualifications are a periodic and  ongoing necessity  qualifications support quality  management systems process validation  mitigate risks results or sample  integrity and provide evidence of  suitability  for the intended use  here are some myths  myth one validation of a process  equipment or instruments  is only done once  in fact no revalidation is required for  process changes reference 21cfr820.70b3  changes to equipment or instrument where  specification changes would trigger a  revalidation  revalidation should be performed if  performance or equipment  or instruments documented in the  qualifications show any deviation or  negative trends  also revalidation should be performed if  there are process failures or kappa  related activities  another myth is validation is only  necessary for processes where subsequent  verification is impossible that's not  true validation should be considered  even if your process include 100  verification 100 verification is not  necessarily 100 effective in a process  in myth 3 validations are burdensome  yes validations can be burdened and  costly but planning is key to mitigation  at this point  validation is also an investment in the  process equipment instrumentation and  personnel it helps you understand the  controls necessary to reduce variability  reducing variability reduces the risk to  results and reduces operational costs  a well-planned process validation  improves customer satisfaction and  confidence  myth four  my field service report or plan  maintenance report is sufficient to  document performance  that's not true to understand  why a service report or maintenance  protocol cannot stand in for a  qualification is because the intent of  the document this is how a potential  investigator will establish the utility  of documentation being performed by a  firm  the intent of service report is to  document the scope of the service event  being performed  a maintenance protocol intention is a  document the manufacturer's recommended  maintenance maintenance activities  activities to be formed  only a qualification is the industry  accepted negative into document  performance as called out in the  guidance documentation from the  international medical device regulators  forum and fda medical device quality  systems  requirements we spoke about earlier in  the webinar  the next two slides are a comparison of  thermo fisher scientific services and  associated details please take note of  the differences here  only the qualification has the intent to  document performance of the instrument  and provide documentation in a formal  signed protocol  in this second comparison slide please  take note of the differences  such as documentation lengths required  time to complete training and  certification  the qualification has significantly  different delivery and requirements  where are qualifications applicable  here is our attempt to align some of the  applicable standards and regulation to  the customer segments that should  consider process validation and  qualification services for thermo fisher  scientific as a manufacturer we will be  looking at part 820 and iso 9001-13485  for some of you in this audience your  interest may align with the clia cap and  iso 15189  but understand these are only some of  the more globally accepted markets for  qualification there will be many local  regional or international government  entities which will also support the use  of a qualification  to document performance of equipment  we recommend using the guidance  documents from global harmonization task  force international medical device  regulators forum and the us fda as  reference starting points  because science can't wait on  non-compliance  i would like to circle back on the  webinar learning objectives  we have summarized where qualification  comes from and the original origin of  the qualification as an industry  standard  we have explained process validation and  how it qual how a qualification fits  we've discussed what thermo fisher  scientific provides in 