king it  making the equipment qualification more  plug-and-play to the validation process  so having the manufacturer perform the  validation  in the long run is the better idea  great we do have another question here  it says  how often should i requalify an  instrument  yeah this is  this is determined by the manufacturer's  recommendation and the risk tolerance of  the workflow thermo fisher uses a  risk-based determination to make  recommendations to requalify  at a minimum  for the lsg instrumentation we recommend  after any move  any pm or plan maintenance or after any  of those critical repairs that i  mentioned earlier that would affect data  so um  that that would be the times that you  would need to re-qualify the instrument  and justin how long does it take thermo  fish or scientific to perform their  qualifications services  yeah great question it varies quite a  bit  for the life sciences instruments  the lsg group it depends on the model or  platform but typically between half a  day  to two and a half days depending on the  platform um and then there is there's  documentation processing that usually  um  follows off-site and uh and then we will  deliver the entire package um you know  the qualification documents as well as  supporting attachments  um at the end of the  service  thank you justin that seems to be all  the questions we have right now at the  moment  so as a reminder to our audience  questions that we did not have time for  today  and even those that are submitted during  the on-demand period  will be addressed via the email address  you provided at the time of registration  so thank you again to our speaker justin  haugen and to everyone who participated  in the presentation we hope you enjoy  the rest of the event and please be sure  to check back frequently for new content  and presentations added throughout the  year  thank you  you

